  "id": "Compound::DB06707 - Gene::151",
  "verbalization": "Levonordefrin is shown to bind to Adra2c, which participates in Alpha2-adrenergic receptor activity, and this activity is participated by Adra2b. Similarly, Levonordefrin binds to Adra2a, which also participates in Alpha2-adrenergic receptor activity, and Adra2b is involved in this pathway. The evidence suggests that Levonordefrin may interact with a receptor subfamily (Adra2a or Adra2c) that is functionally linked to the Alpha2-adrenergic receptor activity, which in turn is associated with Adra2b. The shared involvement of Adra2b in both pathways implies a potential functional overlap, possibly through a common downstream effect. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Levonordefrin influences the activity of Adra2b, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
